title: Assuage Our Partners
subtitle: Accept their liberal economic programme, repair the relationship, replace the government—or refuse.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
frequency: 400
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and left_in_government = 1 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and formation_in_progress = 0 and poland_coalition_affairs_timer <= 0 and government_coalition_dissent >= 40
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_coalition_affairs_timer = 2
card-image: img/poland/cards/coalition-council.webp

= Assuage Our Partners

The coalition council no longer wants another list of Left priorities. The
cabinet's market-liberal and business-aligned ministers demand a broad package
of privatisation, commercial provision and looser labour rules as the price of
restoring a working majority.

We can accept their programme, spend political capacity on the relationship
without conceding policy, or admit that this cabinet has exhausted its
majority and test a named replacement. Refusal leaves the dispute exactly
where it is.

- @liberal_reform
- @ease_relationship
- @replace_government
- @refuse

@liberal_reform
title: Accept a broad liberal reform of the economy
subtitle: Partners rally behind the cabinet; Lewica's polling, unity and social credibility take the cost.
on-arrival: {!
Q.marketisation_concessions += 2;
Q.left_economic_position += 12;
Q.capitalism_acceptance += 8;
Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 24;
for (const partner of ["pis", "ko", "psl", "p2050", "konf"]) {
    if (Q.government_party == partner || Q["ministry_" + partner + "_in_cabinet"]) {
        Q[partner + "_relation"] =
            (Number(Q[partner + "_relation"]) || 0) + 10;
        Q[partner + "_coalition_dissent"] =
            (Number(Q[partner + "_coalition_dissent"]) || 0) - 16;
    }
}
Q.left_poll -= 1.5;
Q.left_poll_momentum -= 0.6;
Q.labor_credibility -= 12;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 5;
Q.workers_support -= 8;
Q.public_sector_support -= 7;
Q.union_trust -= 8;
Q.party_unity -= 7;
Q.razem_dissent += 12;
Q.labor_dissent += 10;
Q.progressives_dissent += 7;
Q.coalition_blur += 10;
Q.government_burden_breached = 1;
Q.news_headline = "Lewica accepts the coalition's broad liberal economic programme";
!}

- #poland_card_finish

@ease_relationship
title: Spend 2 resources to ease the relationship
subtitle: Keep Lewica's programme and buy enough coalition management to cool the immediate revolt.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Whips, joint staff and a new dispute protocol require two resources.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 2;
Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 14;
for (const partner of ["pis", "ko", "psl", "p2050", "konf"]) {
    if (Q.government_party == partner || Q["ministry_" + partner + "_in_cabinet"]) {
        Q[partner + "_relation"] =
            (Number(Q[partner + "_relation"]) || 0) + 5;
        Q[partner + "_coalition_dissent"] =
            (Number(Q[partner + "_coalition_dissent"]) || 0) - 7;
    }
}
Q.government_delivery += 2;
Q.coalition_break_threat = 0;
Q.news_headline =
    "A two-resource coalition protocol eases the relationship without changing policy";
!}

The partners get a dispute calendar, named negotiators and deadlines they can
show their caucuses. Nobody gets the liberal package, but nobody needs to leave
the government this month to prove that the threat was serious.

- #poland_card_finish

@replace_government
title: Bring down the government and find a new majority
subtitle: Open an Article 158 search for a named Prime Minister backed by at least 231 deputies.
choose-if: constructive_vonc_cooldown <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: A failed constructive motion is still inside its three-month constitutional cooldown.
on-arrival: coalition_break_threat = 1; news_headline = "Lewica opens talks for a constructive replacement government"
go-to: poland_government_formation.constructive_motion

@refuse
title: No, we will not do this
subtitle: Skip the demand. The cabinet and its coalition dissent remain unchanged.
on-arrival: {!
if (!Q.left_in_government && Number(Q.month_actions) > 0) {
    // Stale hand safety: do not consume the turn if this governing card was
    // opened after losing office.
    Q.month_actions = Math.max(0, Number(Q.month_actions) - 1);
}
Q.news_headline = "Lewica refuses the coalition's liberal ultimatum";
!}
go-to: poland_card_finish
